   "name": "North Ridge",
   "grade": "Mod. Snow",
   "discipline": "mountaineering",
   "overview": "The route wanders across the low flanks of the peak, close to the East Ridge, then gains the sharp, obvious North Ridge. That ridge runs into a rock band on the East Buttress, which is where roped climbing starts. Climbers can hold left on the crest itself, or aim toward the Crescent Moon Couloir, then curve up and across bare, exposed rock. Either way you exit onto the East Buttress. The summit is reached along the ridge, and the descent is by the West Ridge. Snow cover matters: without it the loose rock band is likely unsafe.",
